{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Narration moved out of the description (P4 admission limit)\n\nThe description crossed the 8000-char plan-review admission cap, so the settled rationale\nlives here instead of in the plan.\n\n**Why option (a) was rejected on cost.** Change `2600` deliberately moved `playwright` to\n`optionalDependencies` and provisions with `--omit=optional` for selections containing no\nbrowser test, cutting the cold install from 15 packages / 30M to 11 / 12M. Option (a) would\nhave re-added that plus a large cached Chromium binary to the critical path of every run.\nrebar's shipped surface is a library, a CLI and an MCP server; the editor bundle's runtime\nbehaviour is not load-bearing enough to buy that on every build.\n\n**What the decision does not concede.** The defect is that absence of execution is\nindistinguishable from coverage. Choosing (b) fixes that by making the non-execution explicit\nAND enforced, not by leaving things as they are. The record is not decorative: without it the\ntier fails. That is the difference between this and \"add a comment saying we meant to\".\n\n**Two review iterations shaped the design.** The first plan-review BLOCKED on G1G2/G6: it found\nthat two browser-tier skip sites outside `conftest.py` — `library_editor_server`\n(`tests/e2e/test_editor_library.py`) and `batch_library_editor_server`\n(`tests/e2e/test_editor_batch_library.py`) — were unenumerated, and that an AST scan scoped to\n`conftest.py` could not see them. Both are now routed through the guard and the scan covers\nevery module under `tests/e2e/`. That finding is worth recording because it is the same shape\nas the original defect: a check whose partition misses a value it was never told about.\n\nFor the same reason the scan was widened a second time, pre-emptively, to `pytest.mark.skipif`\n— the other way a browser test could vanish without ever reaching the fixture guard. There are\nzero uses today, so it costs nothing and closes the class rather than the instance.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788573113023053089,"uuid":"0a94a6b0-09f7-4a08-a943-950d562093f3"}